Z||000000||Elenor84||01-11-2001||12:32 AM||||Hey guys, I own a 84 2m4...the rear defrost switch: there is a little hole were I think there is supposed to be a light...is there?  If so...mine is not working...how do I fix this?  And also...on the air system those dials and knobs...is the background supposed to be lit up...I think it is but I'm not sure...if it is how do I fix it?  Engine is also over heating lots...what do u guys suggest?  Its also -5 degree's Celcius here(I live in canada)...and my gas pedal is like a rock...new throttle cable?  How much will that run me?  Also...I took pic's of my stereo and my car so I will post them very shortly!  thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||01-11-2001||12:49 AM||||no, the little hole is probably where an alarm indicator was........no, the heater indicator is not back-lit.........overheating may be a water pump, or a thermostat, or a coolant leak somewhere in the system.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-11-2001||09:43 AM||||The rear defrost switch in my 85SE has a small light in the switch that illuminates when the defroster is on.  It could be that yours fell out.<P>New switches aren't very expensive from the dealer or from someone like Ed parks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||01-11-2001||10:13 AM||||The defrost and trunk pop switches are back lit when the headlights are on.  The indicator light is inclusive of the switch.  For what I can tell there is no way to remove/replace that indicator light.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>   they have new swithes there also.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
